{title: 314 - Just as I Am}
{artist: Seventh-day Adventist Hymnal}
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: D}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{tag: Gospel}
{tag: }

Verse 1:
[D]Just as I am, [A]without [D]one [A]plea,
[G/B]But that Thy [D]blood was shed for me,
[D/F#]And that Thou [G]bidst me come to [D]Thee,
[A/C#]O Lamb of [D]God, [A]I come, I [D]come.

Verse 2:
[D]Just as I am, [A]and [A7/C#]waiting [A]not
[G/B]to rid my [D]soul of one dark blot,
[D/F#]to thee whose [G]blood can cleanse each [D]spot,
[A/C#]O Lamb of [D]God, [A]I come, I [D]come.

Verse 3:
[D]Just as I am, [A]though [A7/C#]tossed [D]about
[G/B]with many a [D]conflict, many a doubt,
[D/F#]fightings and [G]fears within, without,
[A/C#]O Lamb of [D]God, [A]I come, I [D]come.

Verse 4:
[D]Just as I am, [A]poor, [D]wretched, [A]blind;
[G/B]sight, riches, [D]healing of the mind,
[D/F#]yea, all I [G]need in thee to [D]find,
[A/C#]O Lamb of [D]God, [A]I come, I [D]come.

Verse 5:
[D]Just as I am, [A]thou [A7/C#]wilt [D]receive,
[G/B]wilt welcome, [D]pardon, cleanse, relieve;
[D/F#]because thy [G]promise I believe,
[A/C#]O Lamb of [D]God, [A]I come, I [D]come.

Verse 6:
[D]Just as I am, [A]thy [A7/C#]love [D]I [A]own
[G/B]hath broken [D]every barrier down;
[D/F#]now, to be [G]thine, and thine alone,
[A/C#]O Lamb of [D]God, [A]I come, I [D]come.
